      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=0.5,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[3+2X].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=2$ and $b=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3+2X] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =4\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
